he React config service as the read/write surface so web mode still displays (but disables) desktop-only entries.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_033_agent_and_model_selection.md:36:- A user can define a new agent profile with a custom command line through the config UI and select it at all three levels.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_033_agent_and_model_selection.md:43:- `design\\\\architecture\\\\initial description\\\\config.md`\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\data\\\\local_git_storage_service.ts:13:    ProjectConfig,\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\data\\\\local_git_storage_service.ts:123:    async loadProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference): Promise<Partial<ProjectConfig> | null> {\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\data\\\\local_git_storage_service.ts:124:        return this.requireBridge().loadProjectConfig(project)\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\data\\\\local_git_storage_service.ts:267:    async saveProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference, config: ProjectConfig): Promise<void> {\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\data\\\\local_git_storage_service.ts:268:        await this.requireBridge().saveProjectConfig(project, config)\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_029_search_regexp_agent.md:20:- Implement a `SearchRegexpAgent` backed by the desktop agent bridge: build a prompt asking the configured agent to return only a JavaScript-compatible regular expression for the user's description, run it via the existing agent execution path (`window.md2Actions.runAgent` / F-023 registry), and extract the expression from the output.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_029_search_regexp_agent.md:27:- In Electron mode with a configured agent, entering a description and pressing the agent button replaces the query with a valid RegExp, switches to RegExp mode and shows matching results.\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\github\\\\github_project_config_storage.test.ts:10:    it('loads project config from the repository root', async () => {\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\github\\\\github_project